          %title Prime ideals
          %h1#prime_ideals Prime ideals
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Prime ideals
            are supposed to be a generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
            from elements of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideals"} ideals
            in the sense of ‘ideal elements’ of an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            (usually
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideals"} maximal ideals
            may do a better job. (In particular,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            is
            %em not
            a prime number, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+ideal"} zero ideal
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            is not a maximal ideal either; however, it
            %em is
            a prime ideal.) Nevertheless, they have assumed an importance that dwarfs any question of original motivation; indeed, the general definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+element"} prime element
            follows prime ideals rather than prime numbers. (An element of a ring is prime iff its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal"} principal ideal
            is prime;
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is a prime element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            but not a prime number.)
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          #rig.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
              (assumed unital and associative as usual), and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+ideal"} two-sided ideal
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+ideal"} proper
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x a y
              does for all
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∨
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; (\forall\, a \in R,\; x a y \in P) \;\Rightarrow\; x \in P \;\vee\; y \in P .
            %p
              Also,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong completely prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is proper and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y
              does:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∨
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; x y \in P \;\Rightarrow\; x \in P \;\vee\; y \in P .
          %p
            Note that every completely prime ideal is prime (using that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is unital). The converse holds if the rig is commutative (using that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is an ideal). So in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            one usually uses the (simpler) definition of completely prime ideal as the definition of prime ideal:
          #commrig.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
              rig, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+ideal"} proper
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y
              does:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∨
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; x y \in P \;\Rightarrow\; x \in P \;\vee\; y \in P .
          %p
            Essentially the same definition applies in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+theory"} order theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
            in an order:
          #lattice.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+ideal"} proper
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever their meet does:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∨
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; x \wedge y \in P \;\Rightarrow\; x \in P \;\vee\; y \in P .
          %p
            There is an infinitary version of this that is called ‘complete’ but is
            %em not
            equivalent to the notion in Definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#rig"}
            of a completely prime ideal from the noncommutative theory:
          #complattice.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete lattice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong completely prime
              if some element belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever the meet of a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              does:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∧
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, X \subseteq R,\; \bigwedge X \in P \;\Rightarrow\; \exists\, x \in R,\; x \in X \;\wedge\; x \in P .
          %p
            With a little sublety, this makes sense even when
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meets"} meets
            (and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/joins"} joins
          #preorder.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an ideal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+ideal"} proper
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              that precedes both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              does:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∨
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; (\forall\, z \in R,\; z \leq x \;\Rightarrow\; z \in P) \;\Rightarrow\; (\forall\, z \in R,\; z \leq y \;\Rightarrow\; z \in P) \;\Rightarrow\; x \in P \;\vee\; y \in P .
            %p
              Also,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong completely prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              if some element belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              that precedes every element of a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              does:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∧
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, X \subseteq R,\; (\forall\, z \in R,\; (\forall\, x \in R,\; x \in X \;\Rightarrow\; z \leq x) \;\Rightarrow\; z \in P) \;\Rightarrow\; \exists\, x \in R,\; x \in X \;\wedge\; x \in P .
          %p
            Note that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+filter"} prime filter
            in a proset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a prime ideal in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+order"} opposite order
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^op
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+prime+filter"} completely prime filter
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a completely prime ideal in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^op
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#rig"}
          %p
            All of these definitions may be justified by looking at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantale"} quantale
            of ideals. As discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideals+in+a+monoid"} ideals in a monoid
            %span.newWikiWord
              ideal lattice
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/lattice+of+ideals"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Idl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idl(R)
            a quantale (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I, J
            are ideals, then their product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I J
            is the ideal generated by all products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in I, y \in J
            in the case of rigs, or generated by all meets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \wedge y
            in the case of lattices, or generated by all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            satisfying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \leq x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \leq y
            in the case of general prosets. (Note that for a lattice or other proset,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I J
            is equal to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \cap J
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I J
            suitably defined, every definition above (except the ‘complete’ ones) can be subsumed below:
          #universal.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a rig or a proset, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an ideal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+ideal"} proper
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              is contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I J
              is:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Idl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi J
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Idl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi I
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∨
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, I \in Idl(R),\; \forall\, J \in Idl(R),\; I J \subseteq P \;\Rightarrow\; I \subseteq P \;\vee\; J \subseteq P .
          %p
            Because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I J = I \cap J
            in order theory, prime ideals there are the same as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+irreducible+ideals"} strongly irreducible ideals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+strongly+irreducible+ideals"} completely strongly irreducible ideals
            (generalizing from a pair of ideals to an arbitrary set of ideals). In contrast, the completely prime ideals of noncommutative ring theory are not of much interest; they are a naïve definition that works in the commutative case but not so well in the noncommutative case.
          %p
            Finally, note that most of these definitions have an extra clause that a prime ideal must be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+ideal"} proper
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bias"} bias
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#universal"}
          #unbiased.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a rig or a proset, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an ideal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %strong prime
              if some ideal in the list is contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              whenever the product of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+list"} finite list
              of ideals is contained in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Idl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, n \in \mathbb{N},\; \forall\, I \in Idl(R)^n,\; \prod_{k\in[n]} I_k \subseteq P \;\Rightarrow\; \exists\, k \in [n],\; I_k \subseteq P .
          %p
            As is typical,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            is trivial,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 2
            can be proved from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
            is the mysterious preliminary clause, in this case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is proper. Indeed, the contrapositive of the above implication says that, if none of the
            = succeed "s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
            = succeed "s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_k
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is proper.
          %p
            Note that completely prime ideals in a proset arise by generalizing from finite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            to arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
          %p
            Unbiased versions of the other definitions are fairly straightforward. (For prime ideals in a noncommutative rig, the unbiased definition involves a product of the form
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0 x_0 a_1 x_1 \cdots x_{n-2} a_{n-1} x_{n-1} a_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n
            can be ignored when
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1
            appears in the biased definition. The definition of completely prime ideals in order theory is already unbiased, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            could always be the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
          %p
            Sometimes it's more fruitful to consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of a prime ideal. This is known in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-ideal"} anti-ideal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} tight apartness relation
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
          #constructive.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+with+apartness"} rig with apartness
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a two-sided
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-ideal"} anti-ideal
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is
              %strong prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is
              %span.newWikiWord
                proper
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/proper+antiideal"} ?
              (that is
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x a y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              for some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              do:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; x \in M \;\Rightarrow\; y \in M \;\Rightarrow\; \exists\, a \in R,\; x a y \in M .
            %p
              Also,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is
              %strong completely prime
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is proper and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              do:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
