                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x \in R,\; \forall\, y \in R,\; x \in M \;\Rightarrow\; y \in M \;\Rightarrow\; x y \in M .
          %p
            If we ignore the requirement that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be an anti-ideal, then we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is an
            %strong m-system
            if it is inhabited and satisfies the binary condition of a prime ideal and
            %strong multiplicatively closed
            if it owns
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            and satisfies the binary condition of a completely prime ideal. (A proper anti-ideal necessarily owns
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            In a
            %span.newWikiWord
              matrix ring
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/matrix+ring"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
